{%- comment -%}
  ==========================================================================
  TEMPLATE: Welcome / you are in early (PRELAUNCH VERSION)
  SUBJECT: You are in early
  PREVIEW TEXT: The shop is not open yet. You will be first through the door.
  SEGMENT / AUTOMATION: "Customer signs up" welcome automation (all new
    email subscribers, while the storefront is still password-protected)
  DISCOUNT CODE: none yet. If a founding-subscriber code is created in Admin,
    uncomment the discount row below and put the code in it.
  LAST VERIFIED: not yet test-sent
  ==========================================================================
  Not a theme file. Pasted whole into Shopify Email's custom-code editor.
  Cloned from campaign-shell.liquid; branding is duplicated on purpose, so a
  palette change has to be made in both files. See marketing/emails/README.md.

  THIS VERSION ASSUMES THE STOREFRONT PASSWORD IS STILL ON. Every storefront
  URL currently resolves to Shopify's "Opening soon" password page, so this
  email deliberately does not send anyone there: the wordmark is plain text,
  the footer names the domain without linking it, and the one button points at
  Instagram, which is public. A welcome email whose links all dead-end on a
  password wall is the fastest way to make a new subscriber think the brand is
  broken.

  AT LAUNCH, when the password comes off, change these four things together:
    1. Wrap the header wordmark in a link to {{ shop.url }} (markup below).
    2. Repoint the button at {{ shop.url }}, in BOTH the VML and anchor halves,
       and change both labels to match.
    3. Link the footer's {{ shop.domain }} back to {{ shop.url }}.
    4. Rewrite the "What happens next" section, which is written for a shop
       that has not opened, and update SUBJECT and PREVIEW TEXT above plus the
       preheader div to match.

  The Instagram URL below is hardcoded because Shopify Email has no `settings`
  object. It duplicates `settings.social_instagram_link` in
  config/settings_data.json, and nothing reconciles the two: changing the
  profile URL in theme settings leaves this file stale.

  Deliberately says nothing specific about shipping rates, thresholds, or
  turnaround times. That copy already has four sources of truth (see the
  shipping section of the repo's CLAUDE.md) and an email is a fifth that
  nothing reconciles and that cannot be corrected once sent. It also promises
  no launch date, on purpose: a date that slips is worse than no date.
{%- endcomment -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light">
    <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light">
    <title>{{ shop.name }}</title>
    <style>
      /* Media queries only. Everything else is inline, because Gmail's web
         client drops most of what a style block declares. */
      @media only screen and (max-width: 620px) {
        .ssb-container { width: 100% !important; }
        .ssb-pad { padding-left: 20px !important; padding-right: 20px !important; }
        .ssb-h1 { font-size: 26px !important; line-height: 32px !important; }
        .ssb-button a { display: block !important; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body style="margin: 0; padding: 0; background-color: #e1edf5; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%;">
    <div style="display: none; max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; mso-hide: all; font-size: 1px; line-height: 1px; color: #e1edf5;">
      {%- comment -%} Preheader. Keep in step with the PREVIEW TEXT header line and the editor field. {%- endcomment -%}
      The shop is not open yet. You will be first through the door.
      &#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;
    </div>

    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color: #e1edf5;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center" style="padding: 24px 12px;">
          <table role="presentation" class="ssb-container" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width: 600px; max-width: 600px; background-color: #ffffff; border-radius: 4px;">

            <!--
              Header. The wordmark is plain text while the storefront password is on,
              because {{ shop.url }} is the password page. At launch, wrap the span:
              <a href="{{ shop.url }}" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none;"> ... </a>
            -->
            <tr>
              <td class="ssb-pad" align="center" style="background-color: #071e3f; padding: 28px 32px; border-radius: 4px 4px 0 0;">
                <span style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; line-height: 26px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #ffffff; text-transform: uppercase;">{{ shop.name }}</span>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <!-- Hero text -->
            <tr>
              <td class="ssb-pad" style="padding: 36px 32px 8px 32px;">
                <h1 class="ssb-h1" style="margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 30px; line-height: 36px; font-weight: bold; color: #071e3f;">
                  You are in early
                </h1>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; color: #333333;">
                  Hey {{ customer.first_name | default: 'friend' }},
                </p>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; color: #333333;">
                  Thanks for signing up before there is anything to buy. That is the part we
                  appreciate most, honestly.
                </p>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 16px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; color: #333333;">
                  Sapphire Shadow Studio is a small custom craft studio. We are Maddie and Seth,
                  a husband-and-wife team making embroidered apparel one piece at a time. No mass
                  production, no cutting corners, just pieces we would want to own ourselves.
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <!-- What happens next. Written for a shop that has not opened; rewrite at launch. -->
            <tr>
              <td class="ssb-pad" style="padding: 8px 32px 8px 32px;">
                <h2 style="margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: bold; color: #071e3f;">
                  What happens next
                </h2>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; color: #333333;">
                  The shop is not open yet. We are still finishing pieces, shooting photos, and
                  getting the last details right, because we would rather open a little late than
                  open with something we are not proud of.
                </p>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 12px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; color: #333333;">
                  When the doors open, this list hears first. That is the whole point of it. Until
                  then we will leave your inbox alone: we write when there is something real to
                  show you, and not otherwise.
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <!--
              Optional founding-subscriber discount row. Uncomment once the code exists in
              Admin, and replace LAUNCHCODE with the real code. Do not commit a code that is
              meant to stay private until launch day; this repo is public.
            <tr>
              <td class="ssb-pad" style="padding: 8px 32px;">
                <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color: #e1edf5; border-radius: 4px;">
                  <tr>
                    <td align="center" style="padding: 20px 24px;">
                      <p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; color: #071e3f;">
                        Yours for opening day
                      </p>
                      <p style="margin: 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 22px; line-height: 28px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 2px; color: #071e3f;">
                        LAUNCHCODE
                      </p>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </table>
              </td>
            </tr>
            -->

            <!--
              Call to action. Bulletproof button: VML for Outlook, an anchor everywhere else.
              Points at Instagram, not the storefront, because the storefront is password-gated
              until launch. Keep the two labels and the two hrefs identical.
            -->
            <tr>
              <td class="ssb-pad" align="center" style="padding: 20px 32px 8px 32px;">
                <table role="presentation" class="ssb-button" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                  <tr>
                    <td align="center" bgcolor="#0071C2" style="border-radius: 4px;">
                      <!--[if mso]>
                      <v:roundrect xmlns:v="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" href="https://www.instagram.com/sapphire_shadow_studio" style="height:48px;v-text-anchor:middle;width:300px;" arcsize="9%" stroke="f" fillcolor="#0071C2">
                        <w:anchorlock/>
                        <center style="color:#ffffff;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:bold;">See what we are making</center>
                      </v:roundrect>
                      <![endif]-->
                      <!--[if !mso]><!-- -->
                      <a href="https://www.instagram.com/sapphire_shadow_studio" style="display: inline-block; padding: 14px 32px; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 20px; font-weight: bold; color: #ffffff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 4px; background-color: #0071C2; mso-hide: all;">
                        See what we are making
                      </a>
                      <!--<![endif]-->
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </table>
                <p style="margin: 12px 0 0 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; color: #555555;">
                  Works in progress, finished pieces, and the occasional studio cat.
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <!-- Secondary text -->
            <tr>
              <td class="ssb-pad" style="padding: 16px 32px 36px 32px;">
                <p style="margin: 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 22px; color: #555555;">
                  Already have a project in mind? Custom work is what we like best, and you do not
                  have to wait for opening day to ask about it. Just reply to this email and tell us
                  what you are thinking.
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <!--
              Footer. The domain is plain text while the password is on; at launch, wrap it:
              <a href="{{ shop.url }}" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: underline;">{{ shop.domain }}</a>
            -->
            <tr>
              <td class="ssb-pad" align="center" style="background-color: #071e3f; padding: 28px 32px; border-radius: 0 0 4px 4px;">
                <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; line-height: 20px; color: #ffffff;">
                  {{ shop.name }}
                </p>
                <p style="margin: 0 0 10px 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; color: #c9d8e6;">
                  Questions? Reply to this email, or write to
                  <a href="mailto:{{ shop.email }}" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: underline;">{{ shop.email }}</a>.
                </p>
                <p style="margin: 0; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12px; line-height: 18px; color: #c9d8e6;">
                  You are getting this because you asked to hear from {{ shop.domain }} when it opens.
                  <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color: #ffffff; text-decoration: underline;">Unsubscribe</a>.
                </p>
                {{ open_tracking }}
              </td>
            </tr>

          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
